// PUBLIC SECRETS CONTRACT — an environment's env values and secrets, held by
// the console (encrypted at rest with its field keyring) instead of in sops
// files in the project's repository.
//
// Who may do what is the console's ACL, per method:
//
//   - a person writes values (SetSecret, UnsetSecret) and lists what is SET
//     (ListSecretKeys) — never the values: reading one back is a separate,
//     stepped-up path that is not part of this contract yet;
//   - a deploy reads the values (FetchEnvironmentSecrets), as a machine
//     account whose role grants it, and writes them to the target the way it
//     writes decrypted sops files.
//
// Every write and every fetch is recorded by the console (who, which
// environment, which keys, when). Nothing is deleted: an unset value is kept,
// marked removed, and no longer fetched.
//
// The client does no crypto: values travel over the console's TLS connection,
